From: "Marcelo Poblete (via Claude)" <marcelopoblete.us@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 01:29:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: splice inside the new fiber objects, through to the
 pigtail
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two gaps stopped a splice from being built end to end.

The Splice tab was gated on a hardcoded list of node types — 'Splice
Enclosure', 'Cabinet', 'Handhole' — written before the CE/CTO/Splitter/
ODF types existed. So you could place a Splice Closure and then not
splice in it. The gate now comes from the fiber catalog (does this type
carry an enclosure?) plus whether an enclosure row actually exists at
that node, which also keeps the legacy Handhole rows working and can't
drift the next time a type is added.

The splice matrix patches cable A to cable B core by core, so anything
that is not a cable can never be one side of a splice — and a pigtail
was only a marker. A pigtail IS a short cable in the field: a stub of
fibre, connector on one end, fusion-spliced to the feeder on the other.
Placing one now creates that cable too (12F, 10 ft, matching the
PIGTAIL-CAM-001 rows already in this project), so it shows up in the
matrix and the splice can run through to it. The existing fiber_cables
trigger generates its strands with the TIA-598 colours.

The pigtail cable's failure is reported rather than only logged, same
as the Ductería mirror.

